WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.700
First up,
he's a Peabody Award-winning
Fox News correspondent-at-large,

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:04.303 line:0%
and author of
<i>The Geraldo Show: A Memoir,</i>
Geraldo Rivera!

00:00:04.670 --> 00:00:07.840 line:0%
-(AUDIENCE CHEERS)
-BILL: Hey. How are you?

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:09.142
GERALDO: Good to see you.

00:00:09.208 --> 00:00:12.011
-Been a while. Great to see you.
-Yeah. On the same stage.

00:00:12.178 --> 00:00:15.915
Yes, yes. We--
Well, we shared a stage in 1994,

00:00:16.082 --> 00:00:17.617
-do you remember that?
-That's right. Garry Shandling.

00:00:17.751 --> 00:00:19.786
That's-- Garry Shandling?
Was he on the show?

00:00:20.487 --> 00:00:24.190
-Well, there was thousands
of people on--
-Oh, we shared the same stage.

00:00:24.324 --> 00:00:25.858
-My talk show and your show.
-Oh. Yes. Yes.

00:00:25.958 --> 00:00:28.461
But when I did your show,
Garry Shandling was a guest.

00:00:28.528 --> 00:00:30.096
Oh, well who the fuck
could remember that?

00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:33.265
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)
-I had millions of guests
I could never remember.

00:00:33.399 --> 00:00:36.435
But-- So, uh, your book,
very interesting, and I know--

00:00:36.636 --> 00:00:39.005
Look, I remember you
from<i> Willowbrook</i>

00:00:39.438 --> 00:00:41.374
-I remember when-- Yeah.
-(APPLAUSE)

00:00:41.607 --> 00:00:46.078
I mean, you were the--
one of the original
crusading reporters,

00:00:46.278 --> 00:00:49.749
and you care very much
about your legacy
being as a journalist,

00:00:49.983 --> 00:00:53.919
so I do have to ask,
why Fox News? It's...

00:00:54.053 --> 00:00:55.721
-(AUDIENCE CHEERS)
-Well, that's a fair question.

00:00:55.888 --> 00:00:59.124
I-- I think that
your characterization of Fox
is a stereotype,

00:00:59.224 --> 00:01:00.593
with all due respect.

00:01:00.826 --> 00:01:04.063
I'm-- I'm pro-choice,
I'm pro-immigration reform,

00:01:04.196 --> 00:01:06.232
I'm pro-gun control,
and I'm on Fox News.

00:01:06.466 --> 00:01:10.103
It's easy, because Sean Hannity,
for instance,
is such a big personality,

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:14.474
to say that he represents
the sum total of Fox,
but I-- I think that...

00:01:14.974 --> 00:01:16.109
-BILL: Good.
-...with due respect,

00:01:16.242 --> 00:01:19.846
that there are more voices,
it's not state-run TV.

00:01:20.012 --> 00:01:21.013
-It has a...
-Well--

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:23.582
-...conservative-leaning--
-BILL: Well, come on.

00:01:23.816 --> 00:01:27.119
MSNBC is as liberal,
as progressive
as you could possibly be.

00:01:27.319 --> 00:01:28.822
-Aside for this show.
-But...

00:01:29.755 --> 00:01:32.725
-(APPLAUSE)
-(BILL CHUCKLES)

00:01:32.925 --> 00:01:35.861
-Yeah, we're-- we're HBO. Um...
-(GERALDO LAUGHS)

00:01:36.729 --> 00:01:39.598
But there is a big difference
between MSNBC and Fox News.

00:01:39.698 --> 00:01:41.935
I mean, MSNBC
sticks to the truth.

00:01:42.235 --> 00:01:43.636
-(AUDIENCE CHEERS)
-They-- They--

00:01:43.803 --> 00:01:46.072
-They don't-- They don't--
-(APPLAUSE)

00:01:46.205 --> 00:01:47.506
They don't make things up.

00:01:47.607 --> 00:01:51.344
I mean, Trump--
There's a loop going on,
between Trump and Fox News.

00:01:51.477 --> 00:01:53.813
Would you admit to that?
That he watches Fox--

00:01:53.913 --> 00:01:55.281
I mean, what does he do
all morning?

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:57.149
He doesn't come down
to work till 11:00,

00:01:57.449 --> 00:02:01.754
he's-- he's there,
doing his hair,
watching<i> Fox and Friends,</i>

00:02:01.821 --> 00:02:05.357
(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

00:02:05.457 --> 00:02:07.593
and then he quotes from
<i> Fox and Friends.</i>

00:02:07.794 --> 00:02:10.796
Our policy seems to be
coming from<i> Fox and Friends.</i>

00:02:11.196 --> 00:02:14.100
And then he'll say
something crazy,
and they will back it up.

00:02:14.233 --> 00:02:17.437
I'm still stuck on your saying
MSNBC is the truth.

00:02:18.171 --> 00:02:20.539
No, I'm saying they don't
make things up. They--

00:02:20.673 --> 00:02:23.308
-Russia collusion.
-(AUDIENCE GASPS)

00:02:23.575 --> 00:02:24.677
Where's the collusion?

00:02:24.777 --> 00:02:26.446
-Well, that's what we're inv--
-It's an illusion.

00:02:26.546 --> 00:02:27.713
-It's not collusion.
-Well, first of all--

00:02:28.247 --> 00:02:31.817
First of all, that's what
the investigation is about,
and the report isn't in yet.

00:02:31.951 --> 00:02:33.686
-So you can't say--
-Fourteen, fifteen months.

00:02:33.853 --> 00:02:36.122
-I mean, at what point
do you insist that the--
-But the report--

00:02:36.255 --> 00:02:39.125
When the report comes out.
Come on, Geraldo, you know that.

00:02:39.225 --> 00:02:40.660
When the report comes out.

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:43.562
I'm not saying it's...
it's definitely collusion,

00:02:43.696 --> 00:02:46.265
but you can't say
it's an illusion
until the report comes out.

00:02:46.366 --> 00:02:47.666
-Would you agree to that?
-I--

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:51.737
I say that anyone
who views the witnesses
who have been interviewed,

00:02:51.870 --> 00:02:53.506
-the indictments that
have come down...
-BILL: Wow.

00:02:53.639 --> 00:02:56.008
...the scope of
the investigation so far,

00:02:56.075 --> 00:02:58.544
-has to come to the conclusion--
-BILL: Everybody in
this administration...

00:02:58.678 --> 00:03:00.980
-There's nothing there yet.
-...has been talking to Russia!

00:03:01.046 --> 00:03:02.448
-Are you kidding?
-You would blame them

00:03:02.548 --> 00:03:04.483
if they had Russian dressing
on their salad.

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:06.752
-(AUDIENCE GROANS)
-But they-- What--

00:03:06.852 --> 00:03:08.621
See, this is what I don't get,
is I-- I mean,

00:03:08.788 --> 00:03:12.992
I remember thinking of you
as a crusading reporter who was
fighting against the spin.

00:03:13.192 --> 00:03:14.794
I feel like now
you are the spin.

00:03:14.861 --> 00:03:16.162
-That's so bull.
-(APPLAUSE)

00:03:16.228 --> 00:03:17.597
-That's really so bull--
-Why is that bull?

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:20.666
-Because--
-You really don't see
a Russian connection

00:03:20.766 --> 00:03:24.971
-with the Trumps?
-I absolutely do not.
Where is the connection?

00:03:25.104 --> 00:03:27.907
Give me one-- What's your
best evidence of collusion?

00:03:28.340 --> 00:03:31.977
The Trump Tower meeting
with Don Jr., where they said,
"There was no Russians--

00:03:32.111 --> 00:03:33.746
Oh, wait, there was one.
There was three,

00:03:33.846 --> 00:03:35.214
there was five,
there was eight."

00:03:35.682 --> 00:03:39.152
That-- That meeting,
which is that one that
everyone talks about,

00:03:39.318 --> 00:03:42.488
is-- was so bland
and benign, and stupid.

00:03:42.688 --> 00:03:44.123
Well, you don't know,
you weren't there!

00:03:44.223 --> 00:03:45.958
You only know what they lie
about it.

00:03:46.158 --> 00:03:47.460
You asked me about Fox News.

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:49.228
Let me tell you how
I got to Fox News.

00:03:49.361 --> 00:03:53.532 line:0%
I got to Fox News,
because I'm a native New Yorker,
9/11 happened,

00:03:53.665 --> 00:03:56.769 line:0%
and three thousand
of my friends and neighbors
were killed.

00:03:57.069 --> 00:04:01.773 line:0%
I had a cushy job at CNBC,
the number one-rated show
on that network,<i> Rivera Live.</i>

00:04:02.341 --> 00:04:06.412
I said, "Send me to war."
These sons of bitches
killed all these people.

00:04:06.545 --> 00:04:10.683
Six dads in my children's
grade school were killed
that day.

00:04:11.216 --> 00:04:13.820
NBC said, "We're not gonna
send you to war,

00:04:14.053 --> 00:04:15.621
because your show's
too important,

00:04:15.687 --> 00:04:18.090
we've got plenty of
war correspondents,"
I said, "I quit."

00:04:18.357 --> 00:04:22.762
So I walked away from
a five million dollar payroll,
I took forty percent of that,

00:04:23.196 --> 00:04:25.164
to work as a war correspondent
for Fox.

00:04:25.498 --> 00:04:30.669
From-- From November of 2001,
until 2012,

00:04:31.136 --> 00:04:32.638
basically, that was my job.

00:04:33.072 --> 00:04:36.742
I was a war cor--
Eleven Extended assignments
in Afghanistan,

00:04:36.875 --> 00:04:41.080
eleven in Iraq, Somalia,
every shithole on Earth,

00:04:41.213 --> 00:04:42.715
I went there and covered
for Fox.

00:04:42.915 --> 00:04:46.084
I never got any bad vibes
when I was doing that.

00:04:46.552 --> 00:04:50.089
The war petered out,
it didn't end,
Afghanistan's still continuing.

00:04:50.389 --> 00:04:52.825
We saw what happened with ISIS
in Iraq and Syria.

00:04:54.227 --> 00:04:56.962
So I started doing
more commentary,

00:04:57.062 --> 00:05:00.532
and then, now I get tarred
with the brush,
oh, I'm state TV,

00:05:00.966 --> 00:05:03.068
-or I'm-- I'm the spinner...
-I didn't say you were.

00:05:03.202 --> 00:05:04.770
-I said Fox News is.
-...I'm not-- I'm not--

00:05:04.937 --> 00:05:08.174
No, you-- you accused me
of being the spin that and I--

00:05:08.274 --> 00:05:09.975
Yes. If you-- Okay.

00:05:10.109 --> 00:05:13.245
If you don't see
a connection between Russia
and the Trump organization,

00:05:13.412 --> 00:05:15.114
-I-- I'm sorry--
-I know. I know.

00:05:15.247 --> 00:05:17.283
-But I'll bet you $1000.
-Okay.

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:19.519
(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

00:05:19.886 --> 00:05:21.020
-I'll take it.
-Okay.

00:05:22.054 --> 00:05:25.791
(CHEERING AND APPLAUSE)

00:05:25.991 --> 00:05:28.994
But-- So, I mean,
where Fox News,

00:05:29.128 --> 00:05:30.762
where a lot of
their correspondence is,

00:05:30.929 --> 00:05:33.333
is that Trump is clean,
and Mueller is dirty.

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:35.635
-Well, I--
-That's what they're saying.

00:05:36.002 --> 00:05:40.272
Mueller is dirty. That is--
That is what you see
on a lot of Fox News.

00:05:40.439 --> 00:05:42.808
-Because--
-The opinion shows
in the evening, I agree.

00:05:42.975 --> 00:05:45.244
But Shep Smith in the day time,
Bill Hemmer,

00:05:45.411 --> 00:05:47.312
-those are news guys,
they're straight news guys.
-Okay.

00:05:47.513 --> 00:05:49.815
-Bret Baier in W--
-I'm talking about the shows
in the evening...

00:05:50.015 --> 00:05:51.083
-Yeah.
-...that people watch.

00:05:51.250 --> 00:05:52.484
-Yeah.
-Yeah, those shows.

00:05:52.618 --> 00:05:54.721
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)
-They watch--

00:05:54.921 --> 00:05:56.822
-They watch the daytime too.
-Or the ones in the morning
that Trump watches.

00:05:56.989 --> 00:05:59.125
-So--
-I'm on<i> Fox and Friends</i>
twice a week.

00:05:59.292 --> 00:06:02.561
Okay, but at some point,
it's gonna have to come to that.

00:06:02.828 --> 00:06:05.230
Is Trump dirty,
or is Mueller dirty?

00:06:05.364 --> 00:06:06.999
Where would you say on that one?

00:06:07.166 --> 00:06:09.235
-You think Mueller's dirty?
-I don't-- I can't--

00:06:09.368 --> 00:06:11.270
-I don't wanna speculate that.
-Mueller.

00:06:11.470 --> 00:06:13.105 line:0%
-I don't wanna speculate.
-But Trump, I mean, like, I--

00:06:13.305 --> 00:06:16.842 line:0%
-I think that it is--
-You don't think that this is
a sleazy crime family?

00:06:16.976 --> 00:06:18.010 line:0%
(BILL STUTTERS)

00:06:18.076 --> 00:06:21.814 line:0%
Sleazy and crime aren't
necessarily the same thing.

00:06:21.981 --> 00:06:23.149
-Trump is my--
-No, they're both!

00:06:23.215 --> 00:06:24.383
You know Trump is my friend.

00:06:24.550 --> 00:06:25.818
I've known Trump for 40 years.

00:06:26.385 --> 00:06:28.053
-I don't have--
-I knew OJ!

00:06:28.187 --> 00:06:30.255
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)
-So did Trump.

00:06:30.422 --> 00:06:32.191
-He didn't--
-I interviewed Trump

00:06:32.258 --> 00:06:33.692
-about OJ during the trial.
-He didn't remain my friend...

00:06:33.825 --> 00:06:35.661
when I felt he had
a certain moral lapse.

00:06:35.794 --> 00:06:40.500
Well, in my-- in my family,
my wife agrees with you,

00:06:40.666 --> 00:06:44.904
she doesn't like his policies
on so many things
that I've already listed.

00:06:45.071 --> 00:06:46.739
So she just can't stand the guy.

00:06:47.473 --> 00:06:51.110
I'm different. I can separate
the man who's always been
gracious to me,

00:06:51.277 --> 00:06:53.112
always been nice to my family,

00:06:53.546 --> 00:06:55.547
you know we were on
<i>Celebrity Apprentice</i> together,

00:06:55.714 --> 00:06:56.916
together every day
for six weeks.

00:06:57.116 --> 00:06:59.285
-I've known him, really,
through every--
-Who gives a shit?

00:06:59.418 --> 00:07:01.820
He's running the world now,
what does that matter

00:07:01.954 --> 00:07:04.957
that he was nice to you
at Thanksgiving, Geraldo?

00:07:05.057 --> 00:07:06.392
-(CHEERING AND APPLAUSE)
-I'm not trying to be--

00:07:06.659 --> 00:07:08.260
I'm not trying to be
an asshole to you,

00:07:08.393 --> 00:07:09.929
I'm-- I'm-- This just--

00:07:10.129 --> 00:07:12.231
You're a smart guy,
this befuddles me.

00:07:12.464 --> 00:07:14.933
-I looked up to you.
-(GERALDO STUTTERS)

00:07:15.167 --> 00:07:17.603
You know, if you don't
look up to me,

00:07:17.703 --> 00:07:20.205
because I'm still friends
with the president
of the United States,

00:07:20.339 --> 00:07:22.007
-then shame on you, not on me.
-I don't look up to you,

00:07:22.141 --> 00:07:23.876
because the president
of the United States

00:07:24.043 --> 00:07:25.744
-is doing what he's doing.
-I'm still the person--

00:07:25.844 --> 00:07:28.514
Who-- Who liberated
the developmentally disabled?

00:07:28.648 --> 00:07:29.748
I mean, seriously?

00:07:30.049 --> 00:07:33.085
Who stood shoulder-to-shoulder
with the GIs
in all of those places?

00:07:33.519 --> 00:07:36.455
My friendship with Trump
doesn't diminish me.

00:07:36.955 --> 00:07:39.591
You know, if he's got problems,
you've got problems with him.

00:07:39.758 --> 00:07:40.893
(SCATTERED APPLAUSE)

00:07:41.093 --> 00:07:42.861
Yeah. (LAUGHS)
Okay.

00:07:43.061 --> 00:07:45.631
Um... What do you think
about Stormy Daniels?

00:07:46.065 --> 00:07:47.833
(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

00:07:47.966 --> 00:07:49.068
I'm just, you know-- I--

00:07:49.201 --> 00:07:51.637
Here's what I want--
Not the infidelity.

00:07:51.737 --> 00:07:54.072
Because other presidents
have done infidelity.

00:07:54.273 --> 00:07:58.711
She says that somebody
from the Trump organization
threatened her.

00:07:58.878 --> 00:08:00.612
-Now, we're not saying they did.
-Right.

00:08:00.746 --> 00:08:04.851
-They would have done something.
<i> -The New York Times</i>
ran a headline that said, uh...

00:08:05.952 --> 00:08:11.490
"Adult Film Star Daughter
Threatened by Trump."

00:08:11.857 --> 00:08:13.325
That was the headline,
something like that.

00:08:13.425 --> 00:08:16.328
There was no
"allegedly threatened",
no "supposedly threatened".

00:08:16.461 --> 00:08:18.698
-Okay.
-Trump gets the worst press

00:08:18.831 --> 00:08:21.867
of any president since
Andrew Johnson
in the 19th century.

00:08:22.067 --> 00:08:23.068
He does.

00:08:23.535 --> 00:08:25.204
-Well, because he's not just
the worst--
-I mean, everything he does

00:08:25.271 --> 00:08:27.440
is construed
in the most evil way possible.

00:08:27.573 --> 00:08:28.908
Everything is-- is--

00:08:29.008 --> 00:08:32.377
I mean, like, right now,
African American unemployment's
at record lows.

00:08:32.778 --> 00:08:34.880
Latino unemployment's
at record lows.

00:08:35.047 --> 00:08:38.250
The economy is humming,
people are are 4.1 percent--

00:08:38.350 --> 00:08:40.085
That happened mostly
under Obama.

00:08:40.252 --> 00:08:42.788
-(CHEERING AND APPLAUSE)
-You know that to be true.

00:08:42.922 --> 00:08:44.857
-There's only-- I mean--
-It doesn't work that way.

00:08:44.990 --> 00:08:46.625
It doesn't work that way?

00:08:46.859 --> 00:08:48.394
-He said--
-Yes, you're right.

00:08:48.527 --> 00:08:49.929
Facts don't work that way

00:08:50.062 --> 00:08:51.163
-on Fox.
-Well, that's bullshit.

00:08:51.263 --> 00:08:52.698
That's the facts, Geraldo.

00:08:52.798 --> 00:08:55.300
He's had 14 months
of a thriving economy--

00:08:55.467 --> 00:08:57.736
But when did the recovery start?

00:08:57.869 --> 00:09:02.207
Who was responsible for, like,
turning the economy from
where it was to where it is?

00:09:02.308 --> 00:09:03.642
-You show--
-He continued it.

00:09:03.775 --> 00:09:06.746
You showed him throwing away
his script in West Virginia.

00:09:07.346 --> 00:09:09.715
When I talk to him, I say,

00:09:09.916 --> 00:09:12.885
"Emphasize the things that
you share in common
with most people.

00:09:13.018 --> 00:09:14.386
It's the economy, stupid."

00:09:14.653 --> 00:09:16.789
If you remember
the West Virginia event
yesterday,

00:09:17.022 --> 00:09:18.523 line:0%
there's a woman who stands up
and says,

00:09:18.590 --> 00:09:23.796 line:0%
"Those tax cuts gave me $2000
extra in my family's coffers."

00:09:24.096 --> 00:09:25.097 line:0%
Two thousand dollars.

00:09:25.464 --> 00:09:28.000 line:0%
What Trump should have done,
and what I would counsel him
to do,

00:09:28.167 --> 00:09:33.138
is say, "Yes, and I wanna do
more of that, I wanna help--
A rising tide lifts all boats,

00:09:33.305 --> 00:09:36.141
we're gonna make this country
work for everybody,

00:09:36.375 --> 00:09:39.878
using Republican, uh,
capitalist kinds of principles,

00:09:39.978 --> 00:09:40.979
we're gonna do this--"

00:09:41.079 --> 00:09:42.447
Instead, he goes off
on immigrants

00:09:42.547 --> 00:09:44.416
and he does things
that are very visceral,

00:09:44.649 --> 00:09:46.151
he's very tempestuous,

00:09:46.218 --> 00:09:48.887
his Tweets suck,
I wish I could be
his Tweet editor.

00:09:49.087 --> 00:09:50.489
But I-- I think to...

00:09:50.822 --> 00:09:53.058
When you portray the president
of the United States

00:09:53.125 --> 00:09:54.993
as basically the enemy
of the American people,

00:09:55.093 --> 00:09:56.462
I think that that's
very dangerous.

00:09:56.828 --> 00:09:58.497
Uh... Well,

00:09:59.098 --> 00:10:02.000
he's certainly the friend of
the Russian people,
I'll put it that way.

00:10:02.100 --> 00:10:03.502
-(LAUGHTER AND APPLAUSE)
-But-- But--

00:10:03.569 --> 00:10:07.138
But what I was gonna ask is,
Stormy Daniels contends that--

00:10:07.305 --> 00:10:09.141
-Stormy Daniels is--
-Just let me ask the question.

00:10:09.241 --> 00:10:10.576
Well, let me just
say this. It was--

00:10:10.743 --> 00:10:12.478
-That was--
-Of course you don't want me
to ask the question.

00:10:12.578 --> 00:10:14.746
-Her<i> 60 Minutes--</i>
-Your answer is better than
the question.

00:10:14.880 --> 00:10:18.417
Her<i> 60 Minutes</i> performance
was as empty
as Al Capone's vaults.

00:10:18.784 --> 00:10:21.320
(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

00:10:21.520 --> 00:10:23.121
What did she--
What did she say?

00:10:23.321 --> 00:10:25.090
Forty-five minutes,
they gave her on<i> 60 Minutes.</i>

00:10:25.190 --> 00:10:26.191
-If you'd let--
-Forty-five minutes.

00:10:26.258 --> 00:10:27.359
-(BILL SIGHS)
-Okay, go ahead.

00:10:27.459 --> 00:10:29.795
Can I just ask you
the one question
I was gonna ask you?

00:10:29.995 --> 00:10:31.596
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)
-Just the one.

00:10:32.331 --> 00:10:35.834
She says that someone
from the Trump organization
threatened her,

00:10:36.068 --> 00:10:39.404
came up to her
on the street and said,
"You better shut up about this,

00:10:39.504 --> 00:10:42.942
because it'd be a shame
if your little girl's mother
has something happen to her."

00:10:43.576 --> 00:10:47.312
Look me in the eye and tell me
you think Trump is above
doing that.

00:10:47.545 --> 00:10:49.882
I'm not saying
actually hurting her,
but making that threat,

00:10:50.015 --> 00:10:51.250
sending a goon to do that.

00:10:51.417 --> 00:10:52.784
You don't think Trump
could do that?

00:10:52.851 --> 00:10:54.820
The guy I know
would not do that.

00:10:54.920 --> 00:10:57.089
-He wouldn't do it to you.
-He would not do it to me.

00:10:57.156 --> 00:10:58.690
But, see, this is the OJ thing.

00:10:58.924 --> 00:11:01.694
I-- You know, a lot of--
"OJ was nice to me,"

00:11:01.961 --> 00:11:03.429
-Yeah, he was nice to me--
-You know we had
an OJ Simpson--

00:11:03.595 --> 00:11:05.597
I-- No one knows OJ's case
better than me.

00:11:05.897 --> 00:11:08.400
You know, he had his
bloody fingerprints,

00:11:08.500 --> 00:11:09.668
-you had the--
-That's not--

00:11:09.735 --> 00:11:12.004
The point is that--
That wasn't the thing I--

00:11:12.071 --> 00:11:14.440
-We both agree OJ was guilty.
-But you don't have that
with Russia.

00:11:14.607 --> 00:11:17.109
But the point is a person
can be nice to you,

00:11:17.242 --> 00:11:19.278
-and then be a monster
somewhere else.
-That's true. That's true.

00:11:19.411 --> 00:11:21.347
-Oh, great. I'm so glad
we could agree on that.
-No, that is true.

00:11:21.513 --> 00:11:24.050
(LAUGHTER AND APPLAUSE)

00:11:24.250 --> 00:11:26.852
Okay, I'll just ask
one more thing,
and I'll let you go.

00:11:27.419 --> 00:11:28.820
But just-- The lying.

00:11:29.221 --> 00:11:32.357
It doesn't bother you?
The lying on a scale
we've never seen?

00:11:32.491 --> 00:11:34.160
Just, in that meeting
we were just talk--

00:11:34.260 --> 00:11:36.595
the event we were just
talking about in West Virginia,

00:11:36.728 --> 00:11:39.431
saying that millions of people
voted illegally.

00:11:39.564 --> 00:11:41.867
He's absolutely wrong
about the voter fraud.

00:11:42.001 --> 00:11:44.036
-it's been proven that
he's wrong about it.
-But the lying all the time,

00:11:44.136 --> 00:11:46.371
-about everything,
it doesn't bother you?
-He's wrong about the military

00:11:46.438 --> 00:11:48.740
-to the border.
-It doesn't degrade the country?

00:11:48.807 --> 00:11:52.745
-He has never lied to me
in 40 years.
-To you, OJ! To you!

00:11:54.079 --> 00:11:56.048
But it doesn't--
You can't separate two--

00:11:56.181 --> 00:11:59.151
-You call me OJ one more time,
I'm gonna bop you.
-I'm not saying you're OJ.

00:12:00.119 --> 00:12:02.788
But you're-- You can't
separate those two things?

00:12:02.921 --> 00:12:04.990
I get it, that he has
seduced you personally,

00:12:05.090 --> 00:12:07.092
-you can't overcome that?
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

00:12:07.192 --> 00:12:11.396
You can't overcome that
and see that over here
this man is this other thing?

00:12:11.563 --> 00:12:13.865
You have a malignancy
inside you
when it comes to him,

00:12:13.999 --> 00:12:15.700
where you won't give him
any credit,
and he becomes defensive.

00:12:15.834 --> 00:12:17.269
-I gave him credit.
-He becomes defensive.

00:12:17.469 --> 00:12:22.341
-Let me tell you, Geraldo.
-And he's a real estate broker
and a reality show host,

00:12:22.507 --> 00:12:24.276
he's never had
any political experience.

00:12:24.510 --> 00:12:26.278
There-- He's into braggadocio,

00:12:26.412 --> 00:12:29.782
he's into, you know,
big-- big stuff, you know,

00:12:29.848 --> 00:12:32.384
"Oh, I'm the most famous,
I'm the richest,

00:12:32.517 --> 00:12:34.220
-I'm the tallest,
I'm the most beautiful."
-Okay. All right. Well,

00:12:34.320 --> 00:12:36.621
there are good people
on both sides of this debate.

00:12:36.755 --> 00:12:37.857
-All right.
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

00:12:38.023 --> 00:12:39.658
Thank you so much
for putting up with me,

00:12:39.825 --> 00:12:41.593
and, actually, it was good
to see you again.

00:12:41.693 --> 00:12:44.196
Good luck with the book.
I'm sure the book is good.

